{"coverage":168,"partial":false,"day_closed":true,"window":"00:12–23:46","movers":[],"themes":{"order_wins":["**Waaree Renewable Technologies** -- signs a five-year Operation & Maintenance agreement for a 360 MWp solar power project with an undisclosed Independent Power Producer; value not stated in the cached pages."],"m_and_a":["**JSW Steel** -- the NCLT-sanctioned Scheme of Amalgamation of wholly owned Piombino Steel with and into the Company becomes effective (31-Oct); authorised share capital reclassified, no consideration and no new shares issued.","**Usha Martin** -- completes the slump sale of U M Cables' business undertaking to R R Kabel, effective closing hours of 31-Oct, per the 25-Sep Business Transfer Agreement (filed by both parties; carried once).","**Sai Parenterals** -- Sunday board meeting approves acquiring the remaining 25% of subsidiary SP Analytics (related-party, SP Analytics' own turnover Nil, consideration not disclosed) and records completion of its already-disclosed (11-Aug) 60% acquisition of Saicriti Pharma.","**Arvaya Healthcare** -- completes the acquisition of 100% of the equity share capital of Sushodha Institute of Gastroenterology (SIGPL), approved 24-Oct and closed 1-Nov; consideration not disclosed."],"business_updates":["**Results season** — 13 companies filed results / earnings-call material today (press releases, recordings, transcripts, presentations) — tracked in the Results tab, not itemised here.","**Bharat Coking Coal** -- October raw-coal production rises 7.1% YoY to 2.86 million tonnes; YTD (Apr-Oct) production falls 9.7% YoY to 16.64 million tonnes on a 18.8% YoY drop in overburden removal (per the filing's own figures).","**Coal India** -- October coal supplies cross 70 million tonnes for the first time (70.3 MT, +19% YoY from 59.2 MT), the highest monthly total in its history; October production also a record 67.2 MT (+19% YoY from 56.38 MT).","**Escorts Kubota** -- October tractor sales fall 10.0% YoY to 16,921 units (domestic -10.9%, export +35.7%), while Construction Equipment volume rises 41.6% YoY to 640 machines (per the filing's own figures).","**V.S.T Tillers Tractors** -- October total units fall to 3,519 (power tillers 3,114, tractors 405) from 4,664 a year earlier; YTD (Apr-Oct) units rise to 33,103 from 32,069 -- our arithmetic.","**Hyundai Motor India** -- October total sales (domestic + exports) of 82,299 units, its highest-ever monthly figure, up 17.7% YoY (domestic 62,799 units, +16.7%; exports 19,500 units, +21.1%).","**Tata Motors Passenger Vehicles** -- October sales of 75,426 units, up 23% YoY from 61,295 (domestic PV 73,894 units, +21%; EV sales up 75% YoY to 16,244 units).","**Tata Motors** (commercial vehicles) -- October sales of 47,652 units, up 27% YoY from 37,530 (domestic CV 39,784 units, +13%; international business up 225% YoY to 7,868 units).","**Maruti Suzuki** -- October total sales of 276,120 units, its highest-ever monthly volume (domestic sales also an all-time high of 216,789 units; exports 49,872 units).","**Eicher Motors** -- unlisted subsidiary VE Commercial Vehicles' October truck & bus sales rise 36.2% YoY to 10,587 units (domestic 9,676 units, +36.9%).","**Mahindra & Mahindra** -- October total auto sales of 131,109 vehicles (incl. exports), up 9% YoY, on a record domestic SUV month of 73,338 units (+2%); domestic commercial-vehicle sales up 4% YoY to 33,037 units.","**TVS Motor** -- October sales of 700,134 units, up 29% YoY from 543,557 (two-wheelers 670,679 units, +28%; EV two-wheelers up 120% YoY to 71,382 units; three-wheelers up 60% YoY to 29,455 units).","**SML Mahindra** -- October total sales of 1,065 units, up 1% YoY (cargo vehicles 532 units, +5%; passenger vehicles 533 units, -3%).","**Force Motors** -- October domestic + export sales of 4,104 units, up 44.76% YoY from 2,835 (domestic 4,011 units, +48%; exports 93 units, -25.6%).","**Aavas Financiers** -- crosses Rs 25,000 cr in Assets Under Management; no figure beyond the AUM milestone stated in the cached pages.","**Medi Assist** -- H1 FY27 EBITDA rises 19.0% YoY to Rs 97.2 cr, margin expands 103 bps to 20.3%; PAT up 59.5% YoY (per the filing's own figures; part of the day's results season)."],"distress_risk":["**Jyoti Ltd** -- the Income Tax Department (Vadodara Circle 1(1)(1)) passes a rectification order under Section 154 for AY2020-21 (dated 29-Oct), extending its original Section 147 order already disclosed 31-Mar-2025; financial impact not stated in the cached pages.","**Dion Global Solutions** -- its reconstituted board, now controlled by resolution applicant Indus IntelliRisk & IntelliSense Services (IIRIS) per the 21-Jul NCLT order, meets 3-Nov to record IIRIS's director nominees, the outgoing directors' cessation and the allotment of equity capital to IIRIS under the approved resolution plan.","**Veefin Solutions** -- a disputed step-down subsidiary (Epikindifi Software and Solutions), acting as an operational creditor, files a Section 9 IBC petition against the Company at NCLT Mumbai claiming Rs 1.27 cr; the Company disputes the claim as unsubstantiated and is contesting it."],"other_notable":["**ONGC** -- Reg-30 senior-management change: Executive Director Sanjay Kumar Singh superannuates 1-Nov; Deepali Masirkar (an IPS officer, on deputation) is appointed Executive Director effective 28-Oct.","**Deccan Gold Mines** -- preliminary drilling/modelling at its Bhalukona (Chhattisgarh) project estimates 4 million tonnes of mineralisation at ~0.24% nickel-equivalent grade, covering only ~25% of the identified 1.3 km mineralised corridor -- an exploration update, not a reserve/resource filing."]},"theme_titles":{"order_wins":"Order wins (notable vs mcap)","m_and_a":"M&A / restructuring","business_updates":"Business updates","distress_risk":"Distress & risk","other_notable":"Other notable"},"theme_rows":{"order_wins":[{"pdf_link":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/WAAREERTL_01112026133010_Intimation-s.pdf","declared":t